@startuml HomeShield Sequence Diagram - Intruder
title HomeShield - Sequence Diagram\n"Unknown face appears -> Intruder alert in browser"

skinparam sequenceArrowColor #1E40AF
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #92400E
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #FEF3C7

actor "User\n(browser)" as User
participant "Flask Server\n(server.py)" as Server
participant "CaptureWorker\n(cameras.py)" as Worker
participant "CameraPipeline\n(pipeline.py)" as Pipeline
participant "FaceWorker\n(async thread)" as FaceWk
participant "Models\n(InsightFace ArcFace)" as Models
participant "PersonStore" as People
participant "IntruderStore" as Intruders
participant "EventBus\n(daemon thread)" as EvBus
database "SQLite\n(homeshield.db)" as DB
collections "SSE clients" as SSE

== Live capture loop ==

loop every frame
    Worker -> Pipeline : process_frame(frame)
    Pipeline -> Pipeline : pose + FSM
    alt every fire_every_n frames
        Pipeline -> Models : fire_model.predict()
        Models --> Pipeline : fire boxes
    end
    alt every face_every_n frames
        Pipeline -> FaceWk : submit(frame, ts) (non-blocking)
    end
    Pipeline -> FaceWk : latest_faces()
    FaceWk --> Pipeline : faces (possibly empty)
    Pipeline -> Worker : FrameResult (no event yet)
end

== Unknown face arrives ==

FaceWk -> Models : face_engine.detect(frame)
Models --> FaceWk : list of {bbox, embedding}
FaceWk -> People : gallery()  : list<(id, emb)>
People --> FaceWk : 3 known embeddings
FaceWk -> FaceWk : best_match(query, gallery)\nresult = (None, score=0.21)
note right of FaceWk
  score < threshold (0.42)
  -> no match -> intruder!
end note

FaceWk --> Pipeline : face with match_id = None
Pipeline -> Pipeline : intruder_alert = True
Pipeline -> Intruders : add(embedding, snapshot,\ncamera_id, camera_name)
Intruders -> DB : INSERT INTO intruders
Intruders --> Pipeline : intruder_id
Pipeline -> Pipeline : Build Event(intruder_detected, ...)

== Async event publication ==

Pipeline -> EvBus : publish(event, frame)
note right of EvBus
  publish() returns immediately.
  The capture loop is NEVER blocked
  by disk I/O or network.
end note
EvBus -> EvBus : enqueue
EvBus -> EvBus : (daemon thread wakes)
EvBus -> EvBus : JPEG encode annotated snapshot
EvBus -> DB : INSERT INTO events
DB --> EvBus : event_id
EvBus -> SSE : data: {event_type: 'intruder_detected', ...}

== Browser receives the alert ==

User -> Server : EventSource /events_stream (kept open)
SSE --> User : new event message
User -> User : Toast "Intruder detected on Living Room"
User -> Server : GET /snapshots/<file>.jpg
Server --> User : annotated JPEG
User -> User : Render in event log

@enduml
